{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Output Layer\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 These layers learn patterns and relationships from data.\par
\b Types of Diffusion Models in Generative AI\par
Diffusion Models\b0  are a class of generative models that create data (images, audio, video, etc.) by gradually removing noise from a random signal until a meaningful output emerges.\par
Think of it as:\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent360\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Forward Process\b0 : Add noise to an image step by step until it becomes pure random noise.\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}\b Reverse Process\b0 : Train a neural network to reverse the noise and reconstruct the original image.\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 This technology powers many modern image generators such as Stable Diffusion and DALL\'b7E.\par
\b 1. Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models (DDPM)\par
\b0 DDPM is the foundational diffusion model introduced by researchers in 2020.\par
\b Working\par
Forward Diffusion\par
\b0 Original Image \f2\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Add Noise \f2\u8594?\f0\lang16393  More Noise \f2\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Pure Noise\par
\b Reverse Diffusion\par
\b0 Pure Noise \f2\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Remove Noise \f2\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Clearer Image \f2\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Final Image\par
\b Advantages\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b0 High image quality\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Stable training\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Excellent diversity\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Disadvantages\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b0 Requires many denoising steps\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Slow generation process\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Applications\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b0 Image synthesis\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Medical imaging\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Scientific visualization\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 2. Denoising Diffusion Implicit Models (DDIM)\par
\b0 DDIM is an improved version of DDPM.\par
\b Key Idea\par
\b0 Instead of performing every denoising step, DDIM can skip steps while maintaining quality.\par
\b Benefits\par
\b0\f3\u9989?\f0  Faster image generation\par
\f3\u9989?\f0  Less computational cost\par
\f3\u9989?\f0  Deterministic sampling possible\par
